  "id": "agreement-coefficient",
  "term": "agreement coefficient",
  "definition": "An agreement coefficient is a numerical measure of how closely different raters or coders give the same classifications to the same material. In this context, it is used to judge the accuracy or reliability of coding by showing the level of agreement between reports and assigned codes.",
